Distance-Weighted Distance Scaling: The function applies a standard scaling transformation (Z-score) before computing distances. Because KNN relies entirely on Euclidean distance, scaling ensures that features with larger numerical ranges do not dominate the calculation. Furthermore, by utilizing weights='distance', closer neighboring regions have a much stronger mathematical influence on the imputed value than more distant ones.
4. Mathematical Pipeline Flow
The code automatically handles the entire lifecycle of the data transformation:
Feature Separation: Isolates the refined, post-selection target_columns.
Forward Scaling: Transforms data to a mean of 0 and standard deviation of 1 so distances are perfectly uniform.
KNN Execution: Fills missing entries using distance-weighted coordinates of the closest operational profiles.
Inverse Scaling: Converts the data back to its original physical units, ensuring the final output matches the actual scale of the region's original metrics.
